+### Temporary panels
+
+The optional `temporary-panel` target exposes one versioned JSON request
+method for trusted, user-owned repository panels. Registration is asynchronous:
+`register` returns an operation identity and `status` returns a separate opaque
+registration identity after bounded path and manifest checks. `summon`, `call`,
+`hide`, `unregister`, and `inspect` require that registration identity.
+
+Temporary registrations are process-memory-only. They are not inserted into
+`installedPlugins`, do not change plugin enablement, and do not write
+`shell.json` or `~/.config/omarchy/plugins`. Only manifests with exactly
+`kinds: ["panel"]` are accepted. The panel source runs as unsandboxed code
+inside the shell process. The host rejects noncanonical or symlinked paths and
+rechecks paths and exact manifest bytes immediately before loading. It cannot
+eliminate concurrent same-user replacement races with a URL-based QML Loader.
+Registrations are cleared on shell restart.
+
 **Note on `setPluginEnabled`:** the `enabled` argument is a string. Only the
 literal `"true"` enables the plugin; every other value (including `"True"`,
 `"1"`, `"yes"`, or omitted) disables it. This keeps the IPC surface
